  "articleBody": "Missing a court date for a criminal charge is a really serious situation, and it can create a whole new set of problems for you. It's not just a minor oversight; it has significant consequences that can escalate your legal troubles. Usually, if you miss a court appearance, the judge will issue a bench warrant for your arrest. This means that law enforcement can pick you up at any time, anywhere, and you'll be taken into custody. On top of that, the court can revoke any bail you posted, and you might face additional charges like 'failure to appear,' which carries its own penalties. It's a situation you absolutely want to avoid, and if you accidentally miss a date or know you're going to miss one, contacting your attorney immediately is crucial. They can often communicate with the court, explain the situation, and work to reschedule your appearance or handle the warrant. Don't try to navigate this alone; professional legal help is essential to minimize the damage and get your case back on track.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-26"
